871:
No public street shall become congested with vehicles, people or otherwise so as to prevent the safe and swift operation of public safety vehicles, and the use of public streets shall be subject to the following restrictions and/or requirements:
(1) A block party will be allowed only on minor streets and not directly adjacent to a major or arterial street;
(2) A block party shall not exceed the length of one city block;
(3) A barricade shall be placed at each end of the block designating the block party area and providing adequate warning and notice to motorists that the street is blocked. No vehicular traffic other than emergency vehicles will be allowed to travel inside the barricades during the hours of the block party;
(4) A deposit of $50.00 for the barricades must be made no less than five days prior to the block party; and
(5) No street shall be closed for a block party more than once in a three-month period.
(Ord. No. 2024-2, 5-18-2024)
